EXT. MOONDUST TACOS FOOD TRUCK - NIGHT

A silver food truck sits on a gravel lot under three moons. Steam curls from the grill, and a tiny robot named ZIP wobbles along the counter on caster wheels, juggling a lime, a squeeze bottle and a napkin while LUCY the cook flips tortillas without looking and BIG MO, her towering brother, lifts a crate of glowing peppers over a sleepy dog that snores by the generator. Two teenagers in shiny silver jackets lean on the window and argue about which moon is the best moon.

LUCY
(to everyone)
Okay team, last orders, then we blast off for the next planet!

ZIP
(muttering to self)
Lime, lime, where is the lime... oh. I am holding the lime.

BIG MO
(to Lucy)
Boss, the engine is making that noise again. The sad one.

LUCY
(shrugging)
Then sing it a happy song.

A phone buzzes on the counter. Lucy taps it, and a hologram of GRANDMA TESS flickers above the grill.

GRANDMA TESS (V.O.)
Lucy, sweetheart, are you eating? You sound thin.

LUCY
(to the phone)
Grandma, you can't hear thin.

GRANDMA TESS (V.O.)
I can hear everything. Tell Mo to stop lifting with his back.

BIG MO
(calling out)
I heard that!

ZIP
(to the dog, whispering)
Everybody is so loud tonight.

The dog opens one eye, sighs, and goes back to sleep.
